Testing WOTS+ checksum security...
  Checksum mechanism:
    - Message chunks: values 0 to 15
    - Checksum = sum of (W-1 - chunk_i)
    - If attacker increases a chunk, checksum DECREASES
    - But signature allows only INCREASING chain position
    - Therefore: forgery is computationally infeasible

  Example: chunks = {5, 10, 3, 8}
    Checksum = (15-5)+(15-10)+(15-3)+(15-8) = 34

  If attacker changes chunks[0] from 5 to 6:
    New checksum = 33 (was 34)
    Checksum DECREASED - but attacker can only INCREASE!
  Checksum security test PASSED!

